/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  solverDict -- the recycle plan.  Two cuts, both in the synthesis loop:
  the MATERIAL recycle (Recycle, the separator vapour going back) and the
  ENERGY recycle through the FEHE and the three kinetic beds, cut at
  PreheatedFeed, the FEHE's cold outlet that is bed 1's feed.  The cut was
  HotEffluent until the beds became the CONVERTER sector (DEV.md 4c C69):
  HotEffluent is now that sector's outlet, and a tear cannot be declared on
  a sector's outlet by its plant label (the plan refuses it as an INLET
  TEAR), so the CONVERTER runs before the FEHE and the loop is cut where the
  FEHE closes it.  The converged answer is the same to the recycle tolerance.
  And the tolerance went from 1e-8 to 1e-10 with it: a tear at a REACTOR's
  inlet hands the bed the seed while the energy report reads the FEHE's
  produced stream, so bed 1's own first law shows the tear residual -- at
  1e-8 it was -3.1e-5 kW, above the report's 1e-6 kW floor for a unit with
  no duty, and the run printed ENERGY BALANCE FAILED for a residual that is
  the recycle's, not the bed's.  At 1e-10 the Newton takes 23 iterations
  instead of 18 and the bed closes under the floor.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
tearStreams        ( Recycle  PreheatedFeed );
recycleSolver       Newton;
recycleTol          1e-10;
recycleMaxIter      200;
